✅ Steps to Onboard a New Agency

Research Agency Intake Mechanism

Does the agency offer a public API?

If not, can submission be automated (form‑filling, web automation, PDF + e‑signature)?

What data and documentation does submission require?

What is the expected response / confirmation (ticket number, email, reference)?

Define Agency Schema

Create schema.json describing all required and optional fields (use JSON Schema standard or Pydantic)

Include validations (types, formats, regex, conditional logic)

Implement Module Logic

validators.py: sanitize and validate citizen‑friendly payload

submitter.py: implement submission logic (API call, automation)

status_checker.py: if agency supports status polling or web scraping — implement retrieval

(Optional) escalator.py: implement appeals or follow-up logic

Write Tests

Unit tests: for validation, schema compatibility, transformation logic

Integration tests (mock or real): simulate a submission and, optionally, status check (or mock responses)

Edge‑case tests: missing fields, invalid data, network errors, retries

Document Module

Add README.md in module directory: describe agency quirks, special requirements, known limitations

Provide a .env.template listing required config variables

Add to Plugin Registry

In the central plugin loader (e.g. backend/plugins/__init__.py or registry file), import and register the new module

Assign a unique agency_id for labeling submissions

Instrumentation & Logging

Add metrics: submission success/failure counters, submission latency, retry count

Log structured events: submission attempt, result, errors, status updates — include tracking_id, agency_id, and metadata (but exclude PII)

Deploy & Monitor

Deploy module in dev / staging environment first

Run test submissions, monitor metrics & logs, verify status retrieval works

Once stable, promote to production
